<h2>Chapter 8: Paid Advertising — Google Ads, LinkedIn Ads, and Retargeting for Contractors</h2>
<p>Paid advertising for general contractors requires channel-specific strategies. The same ad that works on Google Search will fail on LinkedIn, and vice versa. Understanding the intent behind each platform is the difference between profitable campaigns and wasted budget.</p>
<h3>Google Ads for Contractors</h3>
<p>Google Ads captures high-intent searches — people actively looking for a contractor right now. For general contractors, the most effective campaign types are:</p>
<p><strong>Google Local Services Ads (LSAs)</strong></p>
<p>LSAs appear at the very top of search results, above traditional paid ads and organic listings. They operate on a pay-per-lead model (not pay-per-click), and leads are typically $20-$50 for home services. Google verifies your license, insurance, and background check before you can run LSAs.</p>
<p>LSAs are particularly effective for remodeling contractors because:<br />
- They display your Google review rating prominently<br />
- You only pay for actual leads (phone calls or messages)<br />
- They appear for high-intent searches like "kitchen remodeler near me"<br />
- They include a "Google Guaranteed" badge that builds trust</p>
