- Discovery ads in Gmail and Google Discover</p>
<p>Budget allocation recommendation: 60% to cold audience acquisition, 40% to retargeting.</p>
<h3>LinkedIn Ads for Commercial Contractors</h3>
<p>LinkedIn is the only platform where you can reliably reach facilities directors, property managers, and development executives. For commercial general contractors, LinkedIn ads should focus on:</p>
<p><strong>Sponsored Content</strong><br />
- Case studies of completed commercial projects<br />
- Whitepapers on commercial construction trends<br />
- "How we solved [specific problem]" content</p>
<p><strong>Lead Gen Forms</strong><br />
- Pre-filled forms reduce friction<br />
- 10-15% click-to-lead conversion rates<br />
- Best for gated content: "2026 Commercial Build-Out Cost Guide"</p>
<p><strong>Message Ads (InMail)</strong><br />
- Personalized messages to targeted prospects<br />
- Use sparingly — overuse damages brand perception<br />
- Best for event invitations or high-value content offers</p>
<p>LinkedIn cost per lead ($75-$250) is higher than Google, but the average commercial project value ($100,000-$500,000+) justifies the investment.</p>
